│     194→
│     195→    where the com_x, ..., L_z are all floating point numbers.
│     196→
│     197→    This can be repeated a total of "timestep" number of times.
│     198→
│     199→    In oxDNA the states are stored in 3'->5' order so we flip the order per strand
│     200→    and need the topology to get the boundaries of each strand.
│     201→
│     202→    Args:
│     203→        path (PathOrStr): path to the trajectory file
│     204→        strand_lengths (list[int]): if this is an oxDNA trajectory,
│     205→            the lengths of each strand, so that they can be flipped to 5'->3' order
│     206→        is_oxdna (bool): whether the trajectory is in oxDNA format
│     207→        n_processes (int): number of processors to use for reading the file
│     208→
│     209→    Returns:
│     210→        Trajectory: trajectory information
│     211→
│     212→    """
