│     116→class LpMetadata(jd_obs.BaseObservable):
│     117→    """Computes the metadata relevant for computing the persistence length (Lp) for each state.
│     118→
│     119→    To model Lp, we assume an infinitely long, semi-flexible polymer, in which correlations in
│     120→    alignment decay exponentially with separation. So, to compute Lp, we need the average correlations
│     121→    across many states, as well as the average distance between adjacent base pairs. This observable
│     122→    computes these two quantities for a single state, and the average of these quantities across
│     123→    a trajectory can be postprocessed to compute a value for Lp.
│     124→
│     125→    Args:
│     126→        quartets: a (n_bp, 2, 2) array containing the pairs of adjacent base pairs
│     127→            for which to compute the Lp
